# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: collect-release-artefact-exceeds-gitlab-size-limit -- collect:release cannot upload a ~1.07 GB set (413)
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: ci-infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-07

* Symptom

The release-2.3.0 tag pipeline (2922308871): collect:release (job 17000128365)
assembled the whole release set -- 15 assets, every platform including the
GitHub-built Windows zips, manifest-release-assets.txt written -- and then
failed at the artefact upload:

#+begin_example
dist/combined/: found 17 matching artifact files and directories
ERROR: Uploading artifacts as "archive" to coordinator... 413 Payload Too Large
FATAL: too large
#+end_example

The set is ~1.07 GB: the two all-platform unions alone are 600 MB
(=clautolisp-2.3.0-all.tar.bz2= 283 MB, =clautolisp-2.3.0-all.zip= 320 MB),
duplicating every per-platform archive beside them. release-2.2.1 was under the
limit; the set grew with the macOS and arm64 binaries and the compiler.

Both publishing scripts read that artefact, so the release could not be
published by the documented procedure.

* Workaround (used for release-2.3.0, now scripted)

Collect locally on poseidon and publish from the local set:
=deploy-release-to-poseidon.sh --from DIR= and =make-gitlab-release.py
--manifest FILE --links poseidon= (AGENTS.md, release runbook). The published
links are poseidon's, so nothing depends on the GitLab artefact.

* Fix options (to decide)

1. Do not upload the =all.*= unions as the artefact: upload the per-platform
   archives + the manifest (~470 MB), and build the unions where they are
   mirrored (deploy-release-to-poseidon.sh runs =make collect-artefacts=, or a
   union step, on poseidon).
2. Drop one of the two unions (=all.zip= exists only "for Windows" and repeats
   =all.tar.bz2=), halving them.
3. Have the pipeline mirror to poseidon itself (a poseidon-tagged job with the
   web-tree access), so the combined set never has to be a GitLab artefact.

=check-release-lane-integrity= / =check-release-artefact-set= must keep
holding whichever is chosen.

* Acceptance

- A release tag pipeline's collect:release succeeds for a set of the 2.3.0
  size, and the documented procedure (deploy, then publish) works unchanged.

* Option 3 chosen and implemented (pjb, 2026-10-24)

pjb: "Creer un compte release-ogamita sur poseidon. Mettre dans son
authorized_keys les cles des utilisateurs qui lui envoient des artefacts
(runner, claude). Donner propriete de /var/www/poseidon/public_html/ogamita a
release-ogamita, groupe www-data; sous-repertoires en 755, fichiers en 644 ou
444 (releases should be read-only). Il n'y a pas d'utilisateurs hors de
poseidon ... Les artefacts crees sur github (windows) doivent etre fetches par
un runner gitlab tournant sur poseidon." Two runners on poseidon: the Docker
one runs as root, the shell one as `runners`.

Done on poseidon (sudo, documentation/setup-deploy.sh, rewritten for it):
- account release-ogamita (/var/lib/release-ogamita); authorized_keys: three
  rrsync forced commands chrooted to /var/www/poseidon/public_html/ogamita --
  the CI key (private half: DEPLOY_SSH_PRIVATE_KEY), claude's and runners'
  ~/.ssh/release-ogamita keys;
- the ogamita tree release-ogamita:www-data, directories 755, files 644,
  release files 444;
- self-tests: each of the three keys writes and lists under
  clautolisp/releases/ and is refused outside the tree; an end-to-end
  re-mirror of release 2.3.0 (claude's key, deploy-release-to-poseidon.sh
  --from) left its archives unchanged, regenerated both index pages, HTTP 200;
- clautolisp-deploy retired (authorized_keys emptied): its CI key was printed
  in a session transcript by a mis-run of the old setup script, so it is
  revoked; the new CI key replaces it.

In the repository:
- collect:release (tags linux/amd64/docker: only poseidon's runners -- so the
  GitHub Windows set is fetched on poseidon) mirrors the set itself on a
  release tag (scripts/mirror-release-to-poseidon.sh), and its artefact keeps
  only the manifest and the release page: no more 413;
- gen-release-index.py --version / --root-index (the sender builds the
  pages; the account runs nothing);
- deploy-release-to-poseidon.sh: --from only (no sudo, the sender's key); its
  default mode would now have emptied a release directory, so it refuses;
- deploy:documentation sends to release-ogamita:autolisp-spec/;
- make-gitlab-release.py --links gitlab documented as pre-2.3.52 only;
- AGENTS.md runbook, poseidon-deploy.md.

Remaining: the first release tag after the merge exercises collect:release's
mirror for real (and deploy:documentation with the new key) -- close then.
Prerequisite: DEPLOY_SSH_PRIVATE_KEY replaced with the new CI key (pjb).
